# Enforce LF line endings for prompt fixtures embedded via include_str!.
# CRLF in these files would break the SHA-256 byte-for-byte parity test
# against the upstream MAGI Python reference.
src/prompts_md/*.md text eol=lf

# Same reason, and the same trap: `include_str!` PRESERVES CR while rustc
# NORMALIZES a string literal to LF, so a needle carrying an escaped CR-LF in the
# source cannot match fixture text loaded from a CRLF checkout. `core.autocrlf` is true on
# the primary development platform, so without this line a fresh clone breaks the
# helpers that mutate these captures -- and the panic names the fixture instead of
# the line endings.
src/providers/fixtures/envelopes/*.json text eol=lf
tests/fixtures/magi_ref_prompts.sha256 text eol=lf
graphify-out/graph.json merge=graphify
